  "ConcurrencyControlNote": "No `If-Match`, `ETag` response header, `If-Unmodified-Since`, or a record-level revision/version field for optimistic-concurrency purposes was found anywhere in the 380-schema merged OpenAPI spec (a direct case-insensitive scan for these tokens across the full spec text found exactly 4 ''etag''-adjacent hits, ALL of which are unrelated false positives on inspection: an unrelated file-upload-part `eTag` field on a multipart-upload schema, two accidental substring matches inside the unrelated schema name `DeleteTagInfo`, and a client-side `CacheBusterParameter` query parameter literally named `etag` used for cache-busting -- NOT an HTTP conditional-write/optimistic-concurrency mechanism. See extract-integration-config-facts.mjs concurrencyControlSignals.etagContexts for the exact matched substrings.). Objects do carry `dateUpdated`/`articleRevisionID`-style informational timestamps/revision IDs (the latter only on Article, for its revision-history feature -- not a general optimistic-lock token), but none is documented as a conditional-write precondition. Any future bidirectional EntityMap must use snapshot-3-way conflict resolution only -- do not recommend MostRecent.",
