  "DeleteSemanticsDetail": "Vendor-wide: HARD delete is the default and dominant pattern -- a real HTTP DELETE verb is documented on 32 of 51 coverable objects (spot-checked directly: DELETE /discussions/{id}, /comments/{id}, /users/{id}, /categories/{id}, /groups/{id}, /roles/{id}, /badges/{id}, /webhooks/{id}, etc.), and none of these objects'' schemas document an accompanying soft-delete/archive/tombstone field (no `isDeleted`/`archived`/`status=deleted` property found on Discussion, Comment, User, Category, or Group). ONE documented, NAMED EXCEPTION: Article has NO DELETE endpoint at all (confirmed absent from /articles/{id}''s operation list, which is GET+PATCH only) -- article deletion/restoration is instead a SOFT, status-based transition via `PATCH /articles/{id}/status` with an explicit enum `{\"undeleted\", \"deleted\", \"published\"}` on the Article schema''s own `status` property. This exactly matches the Webhooks KB article''s own webhook-event description (''A webhook event fires when an article is Added / Edited / Deleted / Restored... when an article is deleted or restored, it fires as an article_update event'') -- i.e. Vanilla''s own documentation independently confirms Articles are restorable (soft-deleted), while a real DELETE-verb object like Discussion or Comment has no such restore path documented anywhere in this evidence trail.",
  "DefaultSyncDirection": "Pull",
