  "DefaultConflictResolution": "DestWins",
  "DefaultConflictResolutionReason": "ConcurrencyControl=none (no ETag/If-Match/version field documented anywhere in the 380-schema merged spec, and the 4 ''etag''-adjacent spec hits are confirmed false positives -- see ConcurrencyControlNote) rules out MostRecent as a safe default, since MostRecent requires a reliable revision/timestamp-of-write signal to arbitrate conflicts that Vanilla does not expose at the API level. DestWins is the conservative default if/when any of the 37 create-capable / 33 update-capable objects is later enabled for bidirectional sync -- it overwrites the MJ destination with Vanilla''s source-of-truth on pull, avoiding silent conflict-loss in either direction until a real concurrency signal is discovered (e.g. via a future live-probe finding an undocumented revision field).",
